WEBVTT

00:00:02.654 --> 00:00:05.701
♪ ♪

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.590
&lt;i&gt;Previously on&lt;/i&gt;
Star Trek: Lower Decks...

00:00:25.764 --> 00:00:27.505
MARINER:
Man, another quantum fissure?

00:00:27.636 --> 00:00:28.593
&lt;i&gt;BOIMLER:
You saw that other Boimler.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:30.508
&lt;i&gt;So cool and successful.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:30.595 --> 00:00:33.381
&lt;i&gt;If I copy him,
then maybe I can be cool, too.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:34.904
&lt;i&gt;RUTHERFORD:
My implant is having&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.558
a hard time connecting
to this old door.

00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:38.603
Well, maybe
it's finally time I fill

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.257
the senior
science officer position.

00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:42.694
You don't think T'Lyn's
competing with me, do you?

00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:44.609
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
I just heard you lost
your captaincy,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.176
and I'm gonna help you
get it back.

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:48.396
&lt;i&gt;MA'AH:
Bargh, I select you to die.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:50.006
Ho, that was awesome, brother.

00:00:50.137 --> 00:00:51.573
We've been assuming
these dimensional rifts

00:00:51.703 --> 00:00:52.965
&lt;i&gt;are a natural occurrence,
but now it's looking&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.358
&lt;i&gt;like someone's making them.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:54.489 --> 00:00:56.273
You have experienced
duplication?

00:00:56.404 --> 00:00:57.753
I mean, if he were still around,
I bet he'd be

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.624
in some huge adventure.

00:01:00.582 --> 00:01:03.193
- Harry, you have to stop.
- [cackles]

00:01:04.238 --> 00:01:06.762
&lt;i&gt;SLOANE:
With a directed soliton burst,
I can guide&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:08.590
the wave into a single reality.

00:01:08.677 --> 00:01:10.505
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
Won't an entire universe
be destroyed?&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:10.679 --> 00:01:12.072
Use my reality.

00:01:12.202 --> 00:01:14.726
&lt;i&gt;I piggybacked a message
to my duplicate.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:14.857 --> 00:01:16.337
- He'll know what to do.
- Will he?

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.556
&lt;i&gt;WILLIAM: Yeah,
as long as he doesn't freak out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:23.605
♪ ♪

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.656
&lt;i&gt;Our scans are negative.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:33.571
&lt;i&gt;There are no enemies
in the area.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:36.096
RELGA:
I can see that.
Set course for the border.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.273
Maybe we can antagonize
Starfleet into a fight.

00:01:39.403 --> 00:01:42.232
&lt;i&gt;But the High Council
considers them to be allies.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:44.104
[bleep] the council!

00:01:44.278 --> 00:01:46.410
We're only patrolling this
worthless corner of the empire

00:01:46.584 --> 00:01:48.108
because my brothers
were murdered

00:01:48.238 --> 00:01:49.587
and the council thinks me weak!

00:01:49.674 --> 00:01:51.937
I would cut all their throats
for a chance to...

00:01:52.068 --> 00:01:55.027
Captain, sensors are detecting
an increase in tachyons.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.900
Tachyons mean nothing
to a Bird-of-Prey.

00:01:57.987 --> 00:02:00.772
[laughter]

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.517
Huh?

00:02:11.261 --> 00:02:13.481
&lt;i&gt;I'm reading a massive buildup
of soliton particles.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:13.655 --> 00:02:15.352
Get us out of here!

00:02:20.836 --> 00:02:22.794
- [shouts]
- [screaming]

00:02:22.925 --> 00:02:25.145
[straining]

00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:36.460
We have evaded the soliton wave,

00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:38.027
but the &lt;i&gt;Krtas&lt;/i&gt;
has been destroyed.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.943
- Shall I report this to command?
- No.

00:02:41.073 --> 00:02:43.641
This is exactly what I needed.

00:02:43.815 --> 00:02:47.254
[laughing]

00:02:48.385 --> 00:02:50.344
♪ ♪

00:03:06.577 --> 00:03:08.840
♪

00:03:43.135 --> 00:03:45.355
♪ ♪

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.935
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
First officer's log.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:00.065 --> 00:04:01.328
&lt;i&gt;Having finished repairs
at a joint&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:01.458 --> 00:04:03.243
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet-Klingon
research station,&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:07.203
&lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is enjoying
a little downtime.&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:07.377 --> 00:04:09.858
Ah. Since we both
have the afternoon off,

00:04:09.988 --> 00:04:12.339
want to play &lt;i&gt;Sexy Treasure
Island&lt;/i&gt; on the holodeck?

00:04:12.469 --> 00:04:14.341
Only if I get to be
Long John [bleep].

00:04:14.471 --> 00:04:16.081
- God, I love you.
- [laughs softly]

00:04:16.212 --> 00:04:18.954
Ah, being a lieutenant JG rules.

00:04:19.041 --> 00:04:21.478
Who knew higher rank came with
more freedom to goof around?

00:04:21.565 --> 00:04:23.175
It's honestly very relaxing.

00:04:23.306 --> 00:04:25.047
That was not your attitude
when I first arrived.

00:04:25.177 --> 00:04:27.179
You were more chaotic.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.051
Really? Ah.
Don't want to lose my edge.

00:04:29.225 --> 00:04:31.140
- Enjoy that avocado, cadet!
- [shouts]

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:33.098
[chuckles] Still got it.

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:34.361
What are you guys so busy with?

00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:35.710
Senior science officer stuff.

00:04:35.797 --> 00:04:37.625
I am cataloging
the corbopple levels

00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:39.844
- of the isometric flangometer.
- And I'm researching

00:04:40.018 --> 00:04:41.759
how corbopple emissions
affect sleep.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.371
C-Corbopple-- you're messing
with me. That's not real.

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.286
- Half of all bopples are corbed.
- It is a foundational element

00:04:46.373 --> 00:04:48.331
- of artificial gravity.
- [grunts]

00:04:48.462 --> 00:04:50.681
- [groans]
- Rutherford.

00:04:50.855 --> 00:04:52.857
I've been trying to fix
this stupid old plasma router,

00:04:52.988 --> 00:04:54.772
which should be easy
with my implant,

00:04:54.903 --> 00:04:56.861
but the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; systems
are too old.

00:04:57.035 --> 00:04:59.516
You love the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;
Don't listen to him, girl.

00:04:59.603 --> 00:05:01.692
- He didn't mean it.
- Yes, I did.

00:05:01.823 --> 00:05:04.260
[sighs] Since when does everyone
bring work to the bar?

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.827
I wish I could help you,
Rutherford,

00:05:05.957 --> 00:05:08.046
but there's not a lot
of engineering advice

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.005
on this PADD I stole
from alt-dimension me.

00:05:10.135 --> 00:05:11.746
I cannot believe
basing your personality

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:13.400
on that thing actually worked.

00:05:13.574 --> 00:05:15.315
That beard looks good.
I hate it.

00:05:15.445 --> 00:05:16.707
I didn't actually crib
all that much.

00:05:16.838 --> 00:05:18.274
Uh-huh.
What do you want to drink?

00:05:18.448 --> 00:05:20.189
Uh, uh, something
called a Bramble?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.408
[device beeping]

00:05:21.538 --> 00:05:23.888
You're getting a message, Boims.

00:05:24.019 --> 00:05:25.629
&lt;i&gt;WILLIAM: No, th-there has
to be something we can do.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:25.803 --> 00:05:27.370
&lt;i&gt;MARINER: Won't you be dooming
an entire universe?&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.458
&lt;i&gt;WILLIAM:
Scan me. Use my reality.&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:28.632 --> 00:05:30.678
Why would you do this
to your friends?

00:05:30.808 --> 00:05:32.854
Sorry, the replicator didn't
have a code for a Bramb...

00:05:32.984 --> 00:05:35.030
Holy [bleep],
we're all gonna die!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.859
What-what the hell? Boims, wait
up! What are we screaming about?

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.427
- [Boimler screaming in distance]
- [glass shattering]

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.124
Is it just me, or is Boimler

00:05:42.254 --> 00:05:43.908
always freaking out
about some PADD?

00:05:44.082 --> 00:05:45.997
- It is not just you.
- [grunts]

00:05:46.128 --> 00:05:48.217
[metal clatters]

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.786
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
T'Pol? Harry Kims?&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:51.873 --> 00:05:54.136
An interdimensional overload?

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.486
Captain, if William's alive,
he wouldn't lie about this.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.619
Mom, I know this is
coming from nowhere

00:05:58.706 --> 00:06:00.098
and we're just junior officers,

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:01.883
but we have to take it
seriously.

00:06:02.057 --> 00:06:03.928
- I agree.
- Oh. You do?

00:06:04.059 --> 00:06:06.670
- Let's get Command
on the line now.
- Whoa, what, really?

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:08.629
I mean, we thought it would take
way more convincing.

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:10.718
Yeah, I mean,
an-an undead transporter clone

00:06:10.848 --> 00:06:12.241
could be kind of a stretch.

00:06:12.328 --> 00:06:13.895
You two are my best officers.

00:06:14.069 --> 00:06:15.331
And after all
we've been through,

00:06:15.462 --> 00:06:16.941
I think I know enough
to trust you.

00:06:17.028 --> 00:06:19.291
Wow. I mean, thanks.

00:06:19.422 --> 00:06:21.642
Man, that is good captaining.

00:06:22.382 --> 00:06:24.514
♪ ♪

00:06:24.688 --> 00:06:26.168
&lt;i&gt;[Ma'ah grumbling]&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:30.694
Eh, why so tense, brother?

00:06:30.825 --> 00:06:33.044
We still have hours
before we arrive at Qo'noS.

00:06:33.175 --> 00:06:35.220
A captain must be vigilant.

00:06:35.351 --> 00:06:37.788
We deliver bloodwine.
What danger would we encounter?

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:39.399
A leaky barrel?

00:06:39.573 --> 00:06:41.662
- Every mission
is a potential battle.
- [yawns]

00:06:41.792 --> 00:06:43.490
Wake me if Kahless
makes another appearance.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:45.274
- [alarm blares]
- [shouts]

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.536
[gasps]

00:06:53.238 --> 00:06:55.545
&lt;i&gt;- [screeching]&lt;/i&gt;
- MA'AH: Relga.

00:06:55.719 --> 00:07:00.245
&lt;i&gt;Ah, the great Captain Ma'ah,
hauling garbage.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:00.376 --> 00:07:01.943
It's not garbage. It's wine!

00:07:02.073 --> 00:07:04.946
&lt;i&gt;How the mighty have fallen,
murderer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:05.076 --> 00:07:06.687
What is the meaning of this?

00:07:06.817 --> 00:07:09.516
You destroyed one of my ships.
I was lucky to survive.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:11.648
&lt;i&gt;We don't know
what you're talking about.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:11.735 --> 00:07:13.650
I know, but there's
just enough truth

00:07:13.737 --> 00:07:15.478
to convince the High Council.

00:07:15.565 --> 00:07:16.784
Ready weapons.

00:07:16.914 --> 00:07:19.177
- This is madness!
- No, it's vengeance.

00:07:19.351 --> 00:07:21.963
Relga has no honor,
just like her brothers.

00:07:22.137 --> 00:07:25.096
&lt;i&gt;Bargh and Dorg were weak.
I am not!&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:25.227 --> 00:07:26.663
&lt;i&gt;Fire!&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:28.012 --> 00:07:29.449
[grunts]

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.149
- [grunts]
- [whimpers]

00:07:34.279 --> 00:07:35.585
I will ram their bridge.

00:07:35.716 --> 00:07:36.978
&lt;i&gt;We will have
the element of surprise.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:37.108 --> 00:07:39.328
Sorry, brother, but today
is not a good day to die.

00:07:39.502 --> 00:07:40.677
[grunts]

00:07:44.028 --> 00:07:45.160
&lt;i&gt;MA'AH:
What are you doing?&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:45.334 --> 00:07:48.729
Unlock my controls now! Malor!

00:07:54.909 --> 00:07:57.302
&lt;i&gt;Long-range scans have confirmed
your fears, Captain Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:57.433 --> 00:08:00.436
&lt;i&gt;Soliton resonance is overloading
the dimensional rift.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:03.831
&lt;i&gt;Unchecked, this will destroy
our quantum reality.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:04.005 --> 00:08:05.746
[all gasp]

00:08:05.876 --> 00:08:08.966
&lt;i&gt;The rift itself is easily sealed
with a subspace gluonic beam.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:09.053 --> 00:08:10.751
&lt;i&gt;The problem is getting to it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:10.881 --> 00:08:12.274
&lt;i&gt;The rift is surrounded&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:12.448 --> 00:08:13.797
&lt;i&gt;by a Schroödinger
possibility field.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:13.928 --> 00:08:15.233
A what?

00:08:15.364 --> 00:08:17.061
&lt;i&gt;The S-field completely
remaps matter&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:17.235 --> 00:08:19.499
&lt;i&gt;into other possibilities
from the multiverse.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:19.586 --> 00:08:21.457
- [all gasp]
- T'LYN: Fascinating.

00:08:21.588 --> 00:08:24.416
&lt;i&gt;Of course, we would never choose
to have a California-class ship&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.157
&lt;i&gt;handle a catastrophe
of this scale.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:26.331 --> 00:08:27.811
Oh, thank God.

00:08:27.942 --> 00:08:29.944
For a moment, it sounded like
this was up to us.

00:08:30.074 --> 00:08:31.772
&lt;i&gt;Unfortunately, it is.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:31.902 --> 00:08:33.382
What?! Why?

00:08:33.469 --> 00:08:35.210
Enterprise &lt;i&gt;is en route,
but there's no time.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:35.297 --> 00:08:37.995
&lt;i&gt;The two Boimlers are linked
in ways we don't yet understand.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:38.126 --> 00:08:41.956
&lt;i&gt;Call it fate or entanglement,
this is your mission.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:42.086 --> 00:08:43.653
How the hell are we
supposed to do this

00:08:43.784 --> 00:08:45.525
if our heads are
turning into cactuses?

00:08:45.699 --> 00:08:48.136
&lt;i&gt;I've calculated adjustments
for your shield harmonics.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:48.266 --> 00:08:50.225
&lt;i&gt;In theory, they should block
the effects of the field.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:50.399 --> 00:08:51.574
&lt;i&gt;Sending them now.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:51.705 --> 00:08:53.707
"In theory"?

00:08:53.881 --> 00:08:55.273
Engineering can make
these updates, Captain,

00:08:55.404 --> 00:08:56.623
but we'll have to work
around the clock.

00:08:56.753 --> 00:08:58.581
It'd be nice to know
if they actually work.

00:08:58.712 --> 00:09:01.410
Come on. Are you sure the
&lt;i&gt;Enterprise&lt;/i&gt; can't handle this?

00:09:01.497 --> 00:09:04.282
&lt;i&gt;With the connected Boimlers,
you're our only option.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:04.413 --> 00:09:06.763
What the [bleep]? You sent
a universe-destroying rift

00:09:06.894 --> 00:09:08.243
to your own dimension?

00:09:08.373 --> 00:09:09.810
It wasn't me. It was William!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.855
Looks like the Boimlers
have given us no choice.

00:09:11.986 --> 00:09:13.378
- [all groan]
- Let's move, people.

00:09:13.509 --> 00:09:15.903
Come on! It was William!

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.600
&lt;i&gt;MEREDITH:
We got to get
those updates installed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:18.949 --> 00:09:20.298
[grunts]

00:09:20.472 --> 00:09:21.473
These plasma conduits
are ancient.

00:09:21.648 --> 00:09:23.432
We're never gonna
flush them in time.

00:09:23.519 --> 00:09:25.303
My implant could do this
twice as fast

00:09:25.434 --> 00:09:27.218
if we didn't have to use
history's oldest relays.

00:09:27.349 --> 00:09:28.437
Got it.

00:09:28.524 --> 00:09:30.482
Quantum filtering is live.

00:09:30.613 --> 00:09:32.354
Shields are updated, Captain,

00:09:32.484 --> 00:09:34.530
but I don't think Starfleet
took into account the hull.

00:09:34.661 --> 00:09:35.792
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN [over comm]:
What? What do you mean?&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:35.923 --> 00:09:37.620
There seems to be
a potential interference

00:09:37.751 --> 00:09:39.666
between the field
and the duranium alloys

00:09:39.796 --> 00:09:41.015
throughout the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:41.145 --> 00:09:42.364
It could affect the hull,

00:09:42.494 --> 00:09:43.844
but the shield updates
should make sure

00:09:43.931 --> 00:09:46.237
that the crew is unaffected,
so we'll all be fine!

00:09:46.324 --> 00:09:47.630
The hull is kind of important.

00:09:47.717 --> 00:09:49.414
&lt;i&gt;BILLUPS:
We're working on a fix.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:49.545 --> 00:09:51.547
&lt;i&gt;- We just need more time.&lt;/i&gt;
- Well, time's in short supply.

00:09:51.678 --> 00:09:54.115
But we should be okay as long as
there aren't any complications.

00:09:54.245 --> 00:09:55.682
[alert blares]

00:09:55.812 --> 00:09:57.161
Captain, a small vessel
just dropped out of warp.

00:09:57.335 --> 00:09:58.162
They're hailing us.

00:09:58.249 --> 00:09:59.860
Damn it. On screen.

00:09:59.947 --> 00:10:01.905
&lt;i&gt;We need to talk
to Beckett Mariner.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:02.036 --> 00:10:03.037
&lt;i&gt;[both grunting]&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:03.167 --> 00:10:04.386
&lt;i&gt;She is my cha'DIch's cha'DIch.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:04.516 --> 00:10:06.127
We are requesting asylum.

00:10:06.257 --> 00:10:08.346
Uh... yeah, hey, guys,
sort of bad timing.

00:10:08.477 --> 00:10:10.435
&lt;i&gt;Good. I do not want asylum.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:10.566 --> 00:10:11.828
&lt;i&gt;- Yes, you do!
- Ugh, I do not!&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:11.915 --> 00:10:14.178
Yeah, I don't know
what they're talking about.

00:10:14.309 --> 00:10:16.616
[groans] Then I guess
we'd better find out.

00:10:16.746 --> 00:10:18.574
&lt;i&gt;MALOR:
Oh, come on.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:18.705 --> 00:10:21.142
We were nowhere near Relga
when her ship was damaged.

00:10:21.272 --> 00:10:23.231
They probably encountered
the same soliton wave

00:10:23.361 --> 00:10:24.885
we're dealing with.

00:10:25.015 --> 00:10:26.974
Relga seeks revenge because
I killed her brothers.

00:10:27.104 --> 00:10:28.584
Uh, yeah, let me just
hop in here.

00:10:28.758 --> 00:10:30.499
Both of those guys tried
to kill him first.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.849
I will gladly die
facing her in battle!

00:10:32.936 --> 00:10:35.156
Come on, she will never
give you a fair fight!

00:10:35.286 --> 00:10:36.766
We can give them safe harbor,
right, Mom?

00:10:36.897 --> 00:10:39.290
Yes, but confined to quarters.

00:10:39.377 --> 00:10:41.771
Sorry, but apparently,
we're the only ones

00:10:41.902 --> 00:10:43.730
who can save
the frickin' universe today.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:46.210
So, do these quarters, um,
have a replicator?

00:10:46.341 --> 00:10:49.344
How do you have an appetite
after running from battle?

00:10:49.474 --> 00:10:51.128
All our snacks are made of bugs.

00:10:51.259 --> 00:10:53.000
They have salties and sweets!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.610
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Captain, we need you
on the bridge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:54.741 --> 00:10:56.525
&lt;i&gt;More Klingons
just dropped out of warp.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:56.656 --> 00:10:57.657
- What?
- Good.

00:10:57.744 --> 00:10:59.049
We don't have time for this.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.095
We're supposed to be
closing a rift.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:12.933
On screen.

00:11:14.021 --> 00:11:15.631
I'm assuming you're Relga?

00:11:15.762 --> 00:11:18.329
I have tracked two murderers
to this location.

00:11:18.416 --> 00:11:19.983
Hand them over now!

00:11:20.114 --> 00:11:22.551
I'm sure we can solve this
in a diplomatic fashion.

00:11:22.682 --> 00:11:24.684
You are harboring criminals.

00:11:24.771 --> 00:11:26.337
They would disagree.

00:11:26.424 --> 00:11:28.775
&lt;i&gt;I know who you are,
Captain Carol Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:28.905 --> 00:11:31.255
&lt;i&gt;Your admiral mate will not
protect you from me.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:31.429 --> 00:11:33.867
My husband has nothing
to do with this.

00:11:33.997 --> 00:11:37.392
You've sided with the &lt;i&gt;petaQs&lt;/i&gt;
who destroyed my ship.

00:11:37.522 --> 00:11:38.959
Are you an accomplice?

00:11:39.089 --> 00:11:41.004
Incoming call from
Admiral Freeman, Captain.

00:11:41.135 --> 00:11:42.266
[sighs] What now?

00:11:42.397 --> 00:11:44.007
Okay. Put her on hold.

00:11:44.138 --> 00:11:45.356
Nobody puts me on hol...

00:11:45.487 --> 00:11:47.358
FREEMAN:
Zo...

00:11:47.445 --> 00:11:48.795
we've partially updated
our shields,

00:11:48.925 --> 00:11:50.710
and we should be able
to head to the rift...

00:11:50.884 --> 00:11:52.581
&lt;i&gt;You're harboring
two criminal Klingons, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:52.712 --> 00:11:54.322
[chuckles] Word travels fast.

00:11:54.452 --> 00:11:56.324
I don't believe
they've committed any crime.

00:11:56.454 --> 00:11:58.021
&lt;i&gt;They're murderers.
I'm ordering you&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:58.195 --> 00:12:00.807
&lt;i&gt;to immediately hand them over
to Captain Relga.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:00.981 --> 00:12:02.156
Dad, these are my friends.

00:12:02.243 --> 00:12:03.592
Is this coming from Command?

00:12:03.766 --> 00:12:05.855
Zo, I...

00:12:05.986 --> 00:12:08.118
- That was weird.
- This whole day is weird!

00:12:08.249 --> 00:12:10.599
[sighs]
Ransom, collect our guests.

00:12:10.686 --> 00:12:12.209
What? No! This is [bleep].

00:12:12.296 --> 00:12:14.646
We can't make our own rules just
because friends are involved.

00:12:14.777 --> 00:12:15.909
Get me that Klingon.

00:12:16.039 --> 00:12:18.607
&lt;i&gt;Freeman! You will rue the day...&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:18.738 --> 00:12:20.957
Enough!
You're getting what you want.

00:12:21.044 --> 00:12:23.046
&lt;i&gt;Ah, there he is.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:23.177 --> 00:12:24.569
&lt;i&gt;No more running, coward.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:24.700 --> 00:12:26.223
- You are the coward!
&lt;i&gt;- Wait.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:26.354 --> 00:12:28.182
Where's the fat one?

00:12:28.312 --> 00:12:30.706
Ransom, why do I only have
one Klingon?

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.056
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Working on it.
Malor seems to have, uh,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:33.187 --> 00:12:34.536
&lt;i&gt;- wandered off.&lt;/i&gt;
- Good.

00:12:34.666 --> 00:12:36.146
This is a trick.

00:12:36.277 --> 00:12:38.670
Sensors can't locate him.
I have a team sweeping the ship.

00:12:38.801 --> 00:12:40.498
Please be patient.

00:12:40.629 --> 00:12:42.326
We're actually dealing
with a dangerous rift

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:43.850
that's emitting strange energy.

00:12:44.024 --> 00:12:46.200
As allies,
I'm sending you the data

00:12:46.287 --> 00:12:47.854
on how to update your shields.

00:12:47.984 --> 00:12:49.943
I have no use for this!

00:12:50.117 --> 00:12:52.989
Give us both brothers
or I will take them by force!

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.298
- [all gasp]
&lt;i&gt;- Hu'tegh!&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:59.169 --> 00:13:00.997
- They're targeting our engines!
- Red alert!

00:13:02.651 --> 00:13:03.521
&lt;i&gt;SHAXS:
Shields at 80%.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:03.652 --> 00:13:05.045
Evasive maneuvers!

00:13:15.664 --> 00:13:17.100
&lt;i&gt;Set a course for the rift.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:17.187 --> 00:13:18.754
- But, Captain...
- We don't have time for a fight.

00:13:18.885 --> 00:13:20.016
Warp me.

00:13:28.546 --> 00:13:30.897
♪ ♪

00:13:32.724 --> 00:13:35.510
I need good news on those
shield updates, Mr. Billups.

00:13:35.597 --> 00:13:37.468
Those Klingons can't be
far behind.

00:13:37.599 --> 00:13:39.035
&lt;i&gt;BILLUPS:
Working on it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:39.166 --> 00:13:40.776
- Mom, I didn't hide Malor.
- FREEMAN: I know.

00:13:40.907 --> 00:13:42.822
But I still need you
to find him now.

00:13:42.952 --> 00:13:45.607
Those Klingons are forcing us
into a bad situation.

00:13:45.737 --> 00:13:47.914
BOIMLER:
We're approaching
the Schroödinger field.

00:13:56.313 --> 00:13:58.054
Captain, without
the shield update,

00:13:58.185 --> 00:13:59.839
quantum interference
with the hull

00:13:59.969 --> 00:14:02.058
could alter the physical
structure of the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:02.189 --> 00:14:03.799
Well, whatever we turn into

00:14:03.886 --> 00:14:06.106
is still better than
getting blown up by Klingons.

00:14:06.236 --> 00:14:07.107
Full impulse.

00:14:07.237 --> 00:14:08.804
Aye, Captain.

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:16.507
RANSOM:
Soliton energy's reacting
with the duranium.

00:14:16.638 --> 00:14:17.857
Readings are getting freaky!

00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:21.034
All hands, brace for weird.

00:14:28.563 --> 00:14:30.870
- Report.
- We only have one nacelle.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.523
We're in the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
from a reality

00:14:32.654 --> 00:14:34.003
where it's a Freedom-class.

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:36.092
How do you even go to warp
with one nacelle?

00:14:36.223 --> 00:14:38.486
It's possible to project a warp
bubble without dual nacelles.

00:14:38.660 --> 00:14:40.444
The only sacrifice is
the static actuators...

00:14:40.531 --> 00:14:41.881
We don't have time to nerd out
about this, Lieutenant.

00:14:42.011 --> 00:14:43.360
- [alert rings]
- Our friends just caught up.

00:14:43.447 --> 00:14:44.579
Of course they did.

00:14:49.453 --> 00:14:51.934
Maintain speed.
We have to get to that rift.

00:14:54.023 --> 00:14:55.851
&lt;i&gt;SHAXS:
The Klingons have entered
the S-field, Captain,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:55.982 --> 00:14:57.766
and our shields are only at 60%.

00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.595
Another energy wave, dead ahead.

00:15:02.814 --> 00:15:04.207
&lt;i&gt;- MA'AH: Malor!
- MARINER: Malor!&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:04.294 --> 00:15:06.209
Get out here right now
so we can face our enemies.

00:15:06.296 --> 00:15:08.255
Would you not?
You're gonna scare him.

00:15:08.385 --> 00:15:10.344
- [ship rumbling]
- [both exclaiming]

00:15:10.474 --> 00:15:13.216
Malor, just-- c-could you get
out here, please, Malor?

00:15:15.305 --> 00:15:17.090
Whoa!

00:15:17.177 --> 00:15:19.527
Dang it! Stupid new quantum
reality power relays.

00:15:19.657 --> 00:15:21.921
- Implant trouble?
- No, it's working great.

00:15:22.095 --> 00:15:23.313
But these new systems
are a mess.

00:15:23.444 --> 00:15:24.575
Who designs a ship like this?

00:15:24.706 --> 00:15:25.968
- [explosion]
- Ah!

00:15:30.755 --> 00:15:32.148
One of their ships is changing.

00:15:37.327 --> 00:15:40.200
&lt;i&gt;Oof, an ancient Klingon
sailing barge.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.331
All lives lost.

00:15:41.505 --> 00:15:42.942
Can that happen to us?

00:15:43.072 --> 00:15:45.248
I could really use
that shield update, Mr. Billups.

00:15:45.379 --> 00:15:47.294
Lieutenant Boimler,
get to navigation.

00:15:47.424 --> 00:15:49.949
We can't afford
to go off course.

00:15:50.123 --> 00:15:52.212
&lt;i&gt;[over P.A.]:
All hands to your stations.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:52.342 --> 00:15:54.040
&lt;i&gt;We need to update our relays.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:54.170 --> 00:15:55.911
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; wasn't designed
for this kind of stress.

00:15:56.085 --> 00:15:58.174
We need to disable
nonessential systems

00:15:58.348 --> 00:16:00.133
to help route power
to structural integrity.

00:16:00.263 --> 00:16:03.353
Negative. Disabling systems
could damage resource conduits.

00:16:03.484 --> 00:16:06.008
Yeah, resource flow won't matter
if we get blown up!

00:16:06.182 --> 00:16:08.097
Raising your voice
will not solve the problem.

00:16:08.228 --> 00:16:09.969
Neither will doing nothing!

00:16:10.143 --> 00:16:11.579
We are co-senior
science officers.

00:16:11.709 --> 00:16:13.015
We should be working
together on this!

00:16:13.146 --> 00:16:14.799
It appears the pressure
of our situation

00:16:14.974 --> 00:16:16.149
- is impairing your logic.
- [gasps]

00:16:16.279 --> 00:16:17.759
Perhaps we should work
on different systems.

00:16:17.889 --> 00:16:19.674
Perhaps we should.

00:16:19.804 --> 00:16:21.981
[grunting, kicking]

00:16:22.111 --> 00:16:24.374
I can't get any of
the isolinear relays stabilized.

00:16:24.548 --> 00:16:26.463
It's this ship. I...

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:29.031
I think I'm falling out of love
with the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:29.162 --> 00:16:31.120
What? But there's
so much more to fix.

00:16:31.251 --> 00:16:32.513
Maybe this is just
a rough patch.

00:16:32.687 --> 00:16:33.862
That's what I thought.

00:16:33.949 --> 00:16:36.604
But it just isn't
getting better.

00:16:47.658 --> 00:16:49.747
- MARINER: Malor?
- This is dishonorable!
Get out here now!

00:16:49.921 --> 00:16:51.401
Malor? Hey, Kimolu, Matt,

00:16:51.575 --> 00:16:53.360
you see a rural Klingon
come in through here?

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.321
Ugh! If I could only find him,
we could stop this conflict.

00:16:58.408 --> 00:16:59.975
Wait. I know I use
this PADD too much,

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:01.933
but maybe something
like this happened

00:17:02.064 --> 00:17:03.457
in Beard Boimler's reality.

00:17:03.587 --> 00:17:04.414
You know what?
Honestly, I'll take any help.

00:17:04.545 --> 00:17:05.850
Check, check.

00:17:06.025 --> 00:17:07.852
- MA'AH: Malor! Malor!
- Whoa.

00:17:07.939 --> 00:17:09.202
You actually found something?

00:17:09.332 --> 00:17:11.465
It's a log about
Klingons seeking asylum.

00:17:11.595 --> 00:17:13.728
- Becky Mariner is the one
who hid them.
- What?!

00:17:13.858 --> 00:17:15.425
Whoa, that doesn't mean I did.

00:17:15.599 --> 00:17:17.340
- She was a piece of work.
- Where is my brother?

00:17:17.427 --> 00:17:19.690
- I didn't hide him.
- This says you did!

00:17:19.821 --> 00:17:21.344
Reveal his location!

00:17:21.431 --> 00:17:24.086
- Guys, guys, can we focus
on repairs?
- [grunts]

00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:29.570
- [rumbling]
- BOIMLER: Whoa.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.180
Look out. We're changing again.

00:17:35.315 --> 00:17:38.274
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is
a Terran Empire ship now.

00:17:38.405 --> 00:17:41.582
Ah, by the prophets,
our weapons are amazing!

00:17:43.323 --> 00:17:45.890
Oh! Weapons are down. Aah!

00:17:47.066 --> 00:17:48.415
Relga, please be reasonable.

00:17:48.545 --> 00:17:50.504
This field is dangerous
as it is.

00:17:50.678 --> 00:17:53.376
&lt;i&gt;You never should have given me
the shield updates, human.&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:53.507 --> 00:17:55.422
&lt;i&gt;Now hand over those fugitives!&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.042
[exclaiming, grunting]

00:18:07.173 --> 00:18:09.697
Tell me we still have shields.

00:18:09.827 --> 00:18:11.177
Barely, but engines are down.

00:18:11.264 --> 00:18:12.656
&lt;i&gt;We're dead in space.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:12.787 --> 00:18:13.918
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
I don't get it.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:14.049 --> 00:18:15.355
&lt;i&gt;Why isn't her ship changing?&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:15.485 --> 00:18:16.921
It probably is.

00:18:17.096 --> 00:18:18.662
Klingons hardly ever update
their fleet designs.

00:18:18.793 --> 00:18:21.187
They always want their ships
to look like big stupid birds.

00:18:21.274 --> 00:18:23.406
We have basic power systems,
but that's it.

00:18:23.537 --> 00:18:25.582
My team's still working
to fix interference,

00:18:25.713 --> 00:18:27.106
but this set us back even more.

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:29.282
We have to assume
we'll be boarded.

00:18:29.412 --> 00:18:31.022
In that case, I think
we have to hand over the...

00:18:31.153 --> 00:18:33.242
- Captain Freeman!
- [exclaims]

00:18:33.373 --> 00:18:36.245
This purple boy has proof that
Mariner has hidden my brother.

00:18:36.376 --> 00:18:38.029
Mom, I wouldn't lie to you.

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.640
I mean, you know, not anymore.

00:18:39.814 --> 00:18:41.381
I know. I trust you.

00:18:41.511 --> 00:18:43.861
Malor's location is hidden
somewhere on this device.

00:18:43.992 --> 00:18:45.211
- [grunts]
- Give me the PADD!

00:18:47.213 --> 00:18:48.692
[grunts]

00:18:48.866 --> 00:18:50.694
&lt;i&gt;- Ba-Qa'!&lt;/i&gt;
- Boims, that thing
was working for you.

00:18:50.825 --> 00:18:52.566
You're so handsome and cool.

00:18:52.696 --> 00:18:54.785
I don't want it in my life if
it means not having your back.

00:18:54.916 --> 00:18:57.136
Oh, man, that's actually--
That's really sweet.

00:18:57.310 --> 00:18:59.050
You're a better friend
than Beard Boimler.

00:18:59.181 --> 00:19:00.487
I don't need a PADD
to know that.

00:19:00.661 --> 00:19:02.141
- Friendship!
- MA'AH: No!

00:19:02.315 --> 00:19:04.055
If you will not tell me
where Malor is,

00:19:04.186 --> 00:19:06.449
I will have to make you,
in battle!

00:19:06.623 --> 00:19:08.364
[growling]

00:19:09.539 --> 00:19:13.282
[pained grunt]
How a-are you s-so strong?

00:19:13.413 --> 00:19:15.502
High intensity
interval training.

00:19:15.632 --> 00:19:16.894
This has gone too far.

00:19:16.981 --> 00:19:18.026
- I hid Malor.
- What?

00:19:18.113 --> 00:19:20.333
- Ha! I [bleep] knew it.
- Why?

00:19:20.463 --> 00:19:22.900
That message from Admiral
Freeman didn't sit right.

00:19:22.987 --> 00:19:25.555
Yes. Thank you.
Mom, it did not sound like Dad.

00:19:25.686 --> 00:19:28.602
We promised Malor asylum,
and Relga's a bully.

00:19:28.732 --> 00:19:30.386
I knew you had to follow orders,

00:19:30.517 --> 00:19:32.780
so I bought you time
and some plausible deniability.

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.521
That wasn't your call, Jack.

00:19:34.608 --> 00:19:37.132
Uzani, when the light
came over the mountain.

00:19:37.219 --> 00:19:39.221
We don't need to watch this.
His orders were clear.

00:19:39.308 --> 00:19:41.528
Jinza, when the truth
was uncovered.

00:19:41.658 --> 00:19:44.966
&lt;i&gt;They're murderers. I'm ordering
you to immediately hand them...&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:45.923 --> 00:19:47.360
Ah, she faked the message.

00:19:47.534 --> 00:19:49.536
Damn. That is so dishonorable.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:52.713
We can't hand them over,
but we can't fight back.

00:19:52.843 --> 00:19:54.584
[sighs]
This is an impossible situation.

00:19:54.758 --> 00:19:55.890
I can't believe
we have Terran weapons

00:19:56.064 --> 00:19:57.805
and no way to power them.

00:19:57.935 --> 00:19:59.981
There has to be some sneaky
underhanded Kirk-style trick

00:20:00.111 --> 00:20:02.505
we can use to [bleep] her up,
like they did in the old days.

00:20:02.636 --> 00:20:05.247
[gasps] One of my officers
might be able to help with that.

00:20:05.334 --> 00:20:07.293
♪ ♪

00:20:10.557 --> 00:20:13.386
&lt;i&gt;Are you really going
to make me board you?&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.953
&lt;i&gt;Save some lives.
Don't be so weak.&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.478
Well, at least I didn't
have to fake a message.

00:20:18.608 --> 00:20:20.131
What? [chuckles]

00:20:20.262 --> 00:20:22.525
A pity you discovered my trick.

00:20:22.656 --> 00:20:24.571
Now your crew has to die!

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.574
You know, you were right.

00:20:27.704 --> 00:20:29.358
I really shouldn't have
shared that shield update.

00:20:29.489 --> 00:20:31.186
Guess I'll just have
to take it away.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:33.493
I'd like to see you try.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.582
[thunder crashing]

00:20:38.237 --> 00:20:39.934
[straining]

00:20:41.675 --> 00:20:42.893
Open fire!

00:20:44.721 --> 00:20:46.245
[shouts]

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.211
It worked!
I did it, Mr. Billups!

00:20:56.342 --> 00:20:58.735
&lt;i&gt;Ha! Your little trick
did nothing!&lt;/i&gt;

00:20:58.822 --> 00:21:00.476
Captain, our shields are down.

00:21:00.607 --> 00:21:02.391
We are fully exposed
to the energy field.

00:21:02.522 --> 00:21:03.827
What? No.

00:21:03.958 --> 00:21:05.655
Fire on them! Destroy them!

00:21:08.528 --> 00:21:09.659
[screaming]

00:21:09.746 --> 00:21:11.444
[groaning]

00:21:11.574 --> 00:21:13.968
[guttural screams]

00:21:14.751 --> 00:21:15.970
[snarling]

00:21:17.885 --> 00:21:19.452
[roars]

00:21:21.192 --> 00:21:22.672
Ugh. What are they turning into?

00:21:22.803 --> 00:21:25.675
Mindless proto-Klingons,
filled with rage.

00:21:25.806 --> 00:21:27.286
&lt;i&gt;[roars]&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:36.512 --> 00:21:38.862
- [alarm beeps]
- Wave frequency is
increasing, Captain.

00:21:38.993 --> 00:21:40.516
All hands, brace for impact.

00:21:44.781 --> 00:21:46.479
[gasps]

00:21:47.697 --> 00:21:49.220
Captain, the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
is operational.

00:21:49.308 --> 00:21:52.485
&lt;i&gt;We've gone all Sovereign-class.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:53.877 --> 00:21:55.488
I guess I'll have to take it.

00:21:55.662 --> 00:21:57.316
Helm, get us to the rift.

00:21:57.446 --> 00:21:59.230
The closer we get, the more
the effects will increase.

00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:00.580
Then let's hope we make it.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:01.581
Full impulse!

00:22:01.711 --> 00:22:04.888
♪ ♪

00:22:25.039 --> 00:22:27.476
Hey! We're back to normal.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:29.260
Yeah, we are.

00:22:29.391 --> 00:22:30.697
[gasps] We are!

00:22:30.827 --> 00:22:32.960
Captain, the rift is
expanding too quickly.

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:34.831
We won't get there in time!

00:22:34.962 --> 00:22:37.181
Why couldn't we have changed
into a bigger, better ship?

00:22:37.356 --> 00:22:39.488
&lt;i&gt;RUTHERFORD [over comm]:
There is no better ship!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:39.575 --> 00:22:41.838
- Rutherford?
- The Cali-class rules!

00:22:42.665 --> 00:22:44.363
We're perfect for this. [grunts]

00:22:44.493 --> 00:22:45.059
&lt;i&gt;TENDI: But I thought you
were falling out of love.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:45.233 --> 00:22:46.626
Yeah, but then I realized

00:22:46.756 --> 00:22:47.888
my problems aren't
with the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:48.018 --> 00:22:49.585
They're with my implant.

00:22:50.934 --> 00:22:52.414
[grunts]

00:22:52.588 --> 00:22:54.111
&lt;i&gt;Time to do this
the old-fashioned way.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:54.285 --> 00:22:56.331
[grunts]
These Calis were designed

00:22:56.462 --> 00:22:57.637
for all sorts of functionality.

00:22:57.724 --> 00:23:00.117
We can reconfigure systems
better than anyone.

00:23:00.204 --> 00:23:03.207
Whoa! I've never seen someone
engineer that fast.

00:23:03.382 --> 00:23:05.514
[chanting]:
Rutherford! Rutherford!

00:23:05.601 --> 00:23:07.647
- Rutherford! Rutherford!
- [beeping]

00:23:07.734 --> 00:23:09.039
He's routing the rift's energy

00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:10.824
directly into
the dilithium chamber.

00:23:10.954 --> 00:23:13.392
We are being fueled by
interdimensionality itself.

00:23:13.522 --> 00:23:15.524
The results
will be unpredictable.

00:23:15.655 --> 00:23:17.221
It'll have to do.

00:23:23.010 --> 00:23:25.534
- [all gasp]
- [echoes]: What's happening?

00:23:27.971 --> 00:23:30.409
Our superpositions
are decoupling!

00:23:30.539 --> 00:23:33.803
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is bifurcating
into two quantum possibilities.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:33.977 --> 00:23:36.066
If we maintain this speed,
they'll both be destroyed.

00:23:36.197 --> 00:23:37.720
We don't have a choice.

00:23:37.851 --> 00:23:39.461
Keep us on course, Mr. Boimler.

00:23:39.592 --> 00:23:41.898
Trying, Captain,
but the helm's not responding.

00:23:42.029 --> 00:23:43.596
SHAXS:
Systems are split.

00:23:43.726 --> 00:23:45.815
[yelps] Each ship is
controlling the other.

00:23:45.946 --> 00:23:48.122
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
We have to slow down.&lt;/i&gt;

00:23:48.252 --> 00:23:49.384
- No!
- No!

00:23:49.558 --> 00:23:51.691
Today's chaos
has driven us apart.

00:23:51.821 --> 00:23:53.649
But that's when we need
to be the most in sync.

00:23:53.823 --> 00:23:55.956
Relinquish control.
Trust each other.

00:23:56.043 --> 00:23:57.958
Before, we had
to prove ourselves.

00:23:58.088 --> 00:23:59.829
Now we unite as...

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:02.049
- Science besties.
- Science besties!

00:24:15.062 --> 00:24:16.803
Wha...?

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:17.978
[group grunts]

00:24:18.108 --> 00:24:19.588
[pants] Brother?

00:24:19.675 --> 00:24:20.763
[group screams]

00:24:23.853 --> 00:24:26.595
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Captain, we're in range!&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:26.726 --> 00:24:27.944
Active the gluonic beam.

00:24:33.384 --> 00:24:34.821
It's not working.

00:24:34.951 --> 00:24:36.562
[alarm rings]

00:24:38.128 --> 00:24:40.827
TENDI:
The rift is still open.

00:24:40.914 --> 00:24:42.524
It's too late!

00:24:45.701 --> 00:24:47.094
On my farm...

00:24:47.268 --> 00:24:48.182
- Huh?
- What?
- ...when a river threatens

00:24:48.312 --> 00:24:49.662
to destroy your crops,

00:24:49.792 --> 00:24:52.926
you cannot stop it,
but you can build a dam.

00:24:53.056 --> 00:24:55.842
- What are you talking about?
- [gasps] He's right.

00:24:55.929 --> 00:24:56.886
[grunts]

00:24:59.846 --> 00:25:01.761
[whirring]

00:25:05.808 --> 00:25:07.897
♪ ♪

00:25:20.823 --> 00:25:23.347
&lt;i&gt;BOIMLER:
Whoa, the energy's contained.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:25.567
The rift is stable,
but it's, uh,

00:25:25.698 --> 00:25:28.135
- it's permanently open.
- Holy [bleep].

00:25:28.309 --> 00:25:30.659
Wait, did we just save
the [bleep] universe?

00:25:30.790 --> 00:25:33.140
[cheering]

00:25:33.270 --> 00:25:37.666
Huh? We are victorious
because you listened to Malor?

00:25:37.753 --> 00:25:39.407
Yeah. Guess Ransom
made a good call

00:25:39.538 --> 00:25:42.062
hiding this big old genius,
or we'd be toast.

00:25:42.149 --> 00:25:44.064
[grunts] Klingons do not hug.

00:25:44.194 --> 00:25:46.936
- [laughs]
- Shut up.

00:25:52.115 --> 00:25:55.075
♪ ♪

00:25:55.205 --> 00:25:57.077
&lt;i&gt;BOIMLER:
Boimler's log.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:57.207 --> 00:26:01.124
&lt;i&gt;Our Klingon friends
are heading back to Qo'noS,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:01.211 --> 00:26:03.518
&lt;i&gt;but they might not
have time for farming.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:03.649 --> 00:26:05.825
&lt;i&gt;Due to her dishonorable actions,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:05.955 --> 00:26:08.175
&lt;i&gt;the High Council handed over
Relga's fleet&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:08.349 --> 00:26:10.438
&lt;i&gt;to Ma'ah's command.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:10.569 --> 00:26:12.614
&lt;i&gt;Now that the rift
is a permanently open portal&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:12.745 --> 00:26:14.442
&lt;i&gt;to other quantum realities,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:14.573 --> 00:26:18.098
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet considers it
a gate to a whole new frontier.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:18.228 --> 00:26:21.797
&lt;i&gt;The increased tachyon density
means no modern starbase&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:21.971 --> 00:26:24.104
&lt;i&gt;can be stationed nearby.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:24.234 --> 00:26:28.195
&lt;i&gt;Luckily, there's one with older
systems that aren't affected.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:28.325 --> 00:26:30.850
&lt;i&gt;Starbase 80.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:32.678 --> 00:26:36.072
&lt;i&gt;The mission:
explore strange new realities&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:36.203 --> 00:26:38.858
&lt;i&gt;with a little help
from some familiar friends.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:38.988 --> 00:26:40.947
&lt;i&gt;Kassia still runs the base,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:41.121 --> 00:26:43.297
&lt;i&gt;but when it comes
to exploring the multiverse,&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:43.427 --> 00:26:44.820
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet wanted their best&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:44.994 --> 00:26:47.780
&lt;i&gt;to supervise the missions
going into the rift.&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:54.221 --> 00:26:55.788
[meows softly]

00:26:58.399 --> 00:27:00.531
It's been an honor, Captain.

00:27:00.662 --> 00:27:03.404
[grunts, strains]

00:27:03.534 --> 00:27:05.188
- [sniffles]
- [groans]

00:27:05.319 --> 00:27:07.713
If you're not here, who's gonna
throw me in the brig?

00:27:08.452 --> 00:27:10.063
When you first arrived,

00:27:10.193 --> 00:27:12.326
I didn't think
you'd last a week.

00:27:12.456 --> 00:27:13.849
Yeah, neither did I.

00:27:13.980 --> 00:27:15.677
- [grunts]
- Now

00:27:15.764 --> 00:27:17.592
I'm proud to say
that you don't need me.

00:27:17.723 --> 00:27:19.550
It's my turn
to go on an adventure.

00:27:19.638 --> 00:27:21.509
[sniffles]

00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:24.686
- I love you, Mom.
- I love you, too.

00:27:30.257 --> 00:27:31.780
Is nobody here to carry my bags?

00:27:31.911 --> 00:27:33.303
Yeah, it's not
a Galaxy-class, Dad.

00:27:33.434 --> 00:27:35.654
- But I'm an admiral.
- So what, your arms don't work?

00:27:35.784 --> 00:27:37.699
I'm glad you guys get to spend
more time together.

00:27:37.830 --> 00:27:40.049
It's the main reason
I agreed to this.

00:27:40.180 --> 00:27:42.008
- There's a golf course, right?
- Oh, forget golf.

00:27:42.095 --> 00:27:43.792
You're hitting the gym, buddy.

00:27:43.923 --> 00:27:45.794
[laughs]:
No, thank you. Not for me.

00:27:45.925 --> 00:27:47.491
&lt;i&gt;FREEMAN:
Well, you're the one
who was calling me every day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:47.666 --> 00:27:48.667
missing me so much.

00:27:48.841 --> 00:27:50.146
Isn't this what you wanted?

00:27:50.277 --> 00:27:52.627
I love you,
but I also love putting.

00:27:52.714 --> 00:27:54.585
Welcome to Starbase 80,
Freemans.

00:27:54.673 --> 00:27:56.109
Now let's get you slimed up

00:27:56.239 --> 00:27:57.893
with some homemade
disinfectant gel.

00:27:57.980 --> 00:28:01.897
- She's kidding, right?
- [laughs] You wish.

00:28:02.724 --> 00:28:04.900
♪ ♪

00:28:06.293 --> 00:28:08.121
Oh, Rutherford.
Hey, will you take a look

00:28:08.295 --> 00:28:10.950
at this data
I compiled for-- what?

00:28:11.124 --> 00:28:12.865
Where's your implant?

00:28:12.995 --> 00:28:15.345
I had to choose between
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; and the oculus.

00:28:15.476 --> 00:28:16.825
Not really a choice at all.

00:28:16.999 --> 00:28:19.132
Uh, I-I, I-I don't know
what to say.

00:28:19.262 --> 00:28:20.699
Engineering should be
twice as interesting

00:28:20.829 --> 00:28:22.309
now that I don't
have cybernetics

00:28:22.439 --> 00:28:23.789
hooked up to my melon.

00:28:23.919 --> 00:28:26.182
It does feel weird
to be so organic, though.

00:28:26.356 --> 00:28:28.707
- Bleh.
- I think you look very handsome.

00:28:28.837 --> 00:28:31.274
Oh! Thanks, Tendi. Wow.
[laughs]

00:28:31.405 --> 00:28:32.798
Emotions can get pretty intense

00:28:32.928 --> 00:28:34.538
without a dopamine
inhibitor, huh?

00:28:34.625 --> 00:28:37.063
- [chuckles] Ooh.
- I was unaware of your
romantic affection.

00:28:37.150 --> 00:28:38.542
Oh, no, we're just friends.

00:28:38.673 --> 00:28:40.153
- My head feels hot.
- What?

00:28:40.283 --> 00:28:42.329
- Am I sick?
- Let me take your temperature.

00:28:42.459 --> 00:28:44.287
[strains, shrieks]

00:28:44.418 --> 00:28:46.420
Clearly I was mistaken.

00:28:46.550 --> 00:28:47.377
[grunts, chuckles]

00:28:47.508 --> 00:28:49.075
[sighs]
What a day.

00:28:49.205 --> 00:28:50.641
Man, whoever decided
to put a bar on a starship

00:28:50.729 --> 00:28:52.208
deserves a medal.

00:28:52.382 --> 00:28:54.820
Mariner, come on,
your mom's leaving the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:28:54.950 --> 00:28:56.996
We had predicted you would
express a negative reaction

00:28:57.170 --> 00:28:59.259
unfitting to the station
of your rank.

00:29:00.303 --> 00:29:03.045
You know why Boimler's
weird death-faking clone

00:29:03.176 --> 00:29:04.830
sent that cosmic wave at us?

00:29:04.960 --> 00:29:07.920
Because he knew we kick ass.

00:29:10.270 --> 00:29:13.403
&lt;i&gt;And I'm not just talking
about the five of us.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:13.577 --> 00:29:17.843
&lt;i&gt;The whole&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;crew is
stacked with amazing officers.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:19.453 --> 00:29:21.629
&lt;i&gt;Yeah, there's a lot of ships
in the fleet which are bigger,&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:21.803 --> 00:29:23.849
&lt;i&gt;fancier, they have
engineering sections&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:23.979 --> 00:29:26.677
&lt;i&gt;that are attached to the main
part of the ship.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:26.808 --> 00:29:30.856
&lt;i&gt;And honestly, those crews
are way more professional.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:31.030 --> 00:29:34.729
&lt;i&gt;Hey, I should know, I've been
kicked out of half of 'em.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:35.774 --> 00:29:39.429
&lt;i&gt;But this thing we do
doesn't require perfection.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:40.691 --> 00:29:42.824
&lt;i&gt;We're explorers.
We live for the unknown.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:42.955 --> 00:29:44.783
&lt;i&gt;You can't prepare for that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:46.697 --> 00:29:50.092
&lt;i&gt;Nobody on the&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos
&lt;i&gt;is even close to perfect.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:50.223 --> 00:29:52.529
&lt;i&gt;We're a mishmash of people
and various creatures&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:54.923
&lt;i&gt;that don't fit in anywhere else.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:57.099 --> 00:29:58.231
&lt;i&gt;But we're a family.&lt;/i&gt;

00:29:58.361 --> 00:30:01.060
&lt;i&gt;That's why I love it here.&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:02.583 --> 00:30:06.413
&lt;i&gt;We believe in the mission
and in each other.&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:06.543 --> 00:30:07.806
&lt;i&gt;My mom might be gone,&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:07.936 --> 00:30:10.983
&lt;i&gt;but she handpicked this crew.&lt;/i&gt;

00:30:13.159 --> 00:30:15.857
Which is why I know
we're gonna be okay.

00:30:15.944 --> 00:30:18.468
This isn't the end of the story,
it's the beginning.

00:30:18.599 --> 00:30:20.122
We're gonna make her proud.

00:30:20.253 --> 00:30:23.125
Wow, that's such a healthy way
of looking at it.

00:30:23.256 --> 00:30:25.388
Yeah. I did get mad
and set my bed on fire.

00:30:25.475 --> 00:30:27.260
- Wait, what?
- What?! Is it still burning?!

00:30:27.390 --> 00:30:29.175
Yeah, and I kicked a computer,
but you know,

00:30:29.349 --> 00:30:31.090
that's all out of my system.
I'm good, I think.

00:30:31.220 --> 00:30:32.743
I m-- I mean, I don't know.
We'll have to wait and see.

00:30:32.874 --> 00:30:34.658
[chuckles]
Tune in. Uh-oh.

00:30:34.789 --> 00:30:36.835
SHAXS:
Captain on deck.

00:30:36.965 --> 00:30:39.968
♪ ♪

00:30:40.099 --> 00:30:41.970
Captain Freeman's
aboard Starbase 80,

00:30:42.101 --> 00:30:44.494
- Captain Ransom.
- Thank you, Mr. Shaxs.

00:30:44.625 --> 00:30:47.541
You know, she told me to never
let you detonate the warp core.

00:30:47.628 --> 00:30:49.499
Oh, man.

00:30:49.630 --> 00:30:51.893
- Unless you really deserve it.
- All right!

00:30:52.024 --> 00:30:53.982
Mr. Rutherford,
a little birdie told me

00:30:54.156 --> 00:30:56.942
you made some pretty inspired
updates to the plasma injectors.

00:30:57.072 --> 00:30:58.552
Was it Dr. Migleemo?

00:30:58.682 --> 00:31:00.510
Yes, it was.
Keep up the good work.

00:31:00.641 --> 00:31:01.947
- Okey dokey.
- Starfleet wants us

00:31:02.077 --> 00:31:05.254
to check out some talking goo
on Snickmik 5.

00:31:05.341 --> 00:31:06.734
What viscosity is the goo?

00:31:06.865 --> 00:31:08.344
Ooh, does it have
anything nice to say?

00:31:08.431 --> 00:31:09.650
Let's find out.

00:31:09.780 --> 00:31:11.217
Helm, take us out.

00:31:11.347 --> 00:31:13.610
♪ ♪

00:31:21.444 --> 00:31:24.143
Hey, Jack. Uh, I mean, Captain.

00:31:24.273 --> 00:31:25.709
Is this gonna be a problem?

00:31:25.884 --> 00:31:27.537
Nah, you're &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; strong.

00:31:27.668 --> 00:31:29.148
Boimler, huddle up with us.

00:31:29.322 --> 00:31:31.890
Huddle up? Oh, no,
we're not doing coach talk.

00:31:32.020 --> 00:31:33.979
I need a first officer.

00:31:34.153 --> 00:31:36.720
[gasps] Bu-- uh,
but I'm only a lieutenant JG.

00:31:36.807 --> 00:31:38.592
[chuckles]
I know you're not quite ready,

00:31:38.722 --> 00:31:40.942
but the two of you have a chance
of making it work

00:31:41.073 --> 00:31:42.813
as provisional first officers.

00:31:42.901 --> 00:31:44.119
What?

00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:46.078
- That's not a thing.
- It is now.

00:31:46.165 --> 00:31:47.818
I might eventually promote
one of you.

00:31:47.993 --> 00:31:50.125
- Think of it as a contest.
- Please don't do this.

00:31:50.256 --> 00:31:51.474
It will mess up our friendship.

00:31:51.561 --> 00:31:52.736
Eh, a little
interpersonal conflict's

00:31:52.867 --> 00:31:53.912
the best way to learn.

00:31:54.086 --> 00:31:55.783
- Since when?
- Sir, but I-I can't.

00:31:55.957 --> 00:31:57.567
I don't-- we're still
lower decks.

00:31:57.741 --> 00:31:59.656
No, you're in charge
of the lower decks.

00:31:59.787 --> 00:32:00.919
Grab a seat.

00:32:01.049 --> 00:32:02.268
[whimpers]
Oh, man.

00:32:02.442 --> 00:32:04.139
[groans]

00:32:08.491 --> 00:32:10.754
♪ ♪

00:32:14.149 --> 00:32:15.194
&lt;i&gt;RANSOM:
Oh,&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:15.324 --> 00:32:16.282
I got to figure out a cool thing

00:32:16.412 --> 00:32:17.848
to say when we go to warp.

00:32:17.979 --> 00:32:19.850
I-I think it'll happen
naturally, over time.

00:32:20.025 --> 00:32:21.678
Yeah, you don't want it
to sound forced.

00:32:21.809 --> 00:32:24.203
Ooh, I got one. Engage the core.

00:32:24.290 --> 00:32:25.639
- Uh, no. I don't like it.
- No, no. Don't you dare

00:32:25.769 --> 00:32:27.728
- go to warp on a workout joke.
- Nope, I'm sorry,

00:32:27.858 --> 00:32:29.599
&lt;i&gt;- I like it. It's staying.
- Ransom, you are better
than this.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:29.730 --> 00:32:31.427
&lt;i&gt;BOIMLER:
No, please
don't make this our lives, sir.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:31.601 --> 00:32:33.386
&lt;i&gt;MARINER:
Come on, you don't want
to set that tone.&lt;/i&gt;

00:32:33.516 --> 00:32:35.649
&lt;i&gt;- BOIMLER: Sir...
- What if this is
a five-year mission?&lt;/i&gt;

